ecords a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-supported-dichotomy"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-supported-dichotomy"],"id":"long.thm-supported-dichotomy","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 1.9 (Support-restricted refinement)","locator":"Long record Theorem 1.9, p. 23, label thm:supported-dichotomy","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Use zero-based indices in this statement: coordinate $j\\in\\mathbb{N}$ carries weight $w_{j+1}$. For $J\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}$, consider the sums that use only coordinates in $J$. If $\\mathbb{N}\\smallsetminus J$ is finite, this achievement set has measure $2^{-|\\mathbb{N}\\smallsetminus J|}$; if infinitely many coordinates are omitted, its measure is zero. Injectivity survives every restriction; perfectness is proved when $J$ is infinite. No perfectness claim is made for finite $J$, whose coding range is finite.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-supported-dichotomy","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-supported-dichotomy","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-supported-dichotomy%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.perfect_supportedMersenneAchievementSet%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-supported-dichotomy%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.perfect_supportedMersenneAchievementSet%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.perfect_supportedMersenneAchievementSet"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments",